From: Arve Hjønnevåg
Subject: ARM: decompressor: invalidate the TLB after switching TTBR0

Adapt the one-line ARMv7 change discussed in the original upstream patch
to Linux 6.12.118. The Exynos5420 Galaxy Tab device tree identifies it as
needed for the stock Samsung bootloader. Keep the existing VMSA guard.

Original submission: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2012/12/12/55

--- a/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/compressed/head.S
@@ -885,6 +885,7 @@
 		bic     r6, r6, #1 << 31        @ 32-bit translation system
 		bic     r6, r6, #(7 << 0) | (1 << 4)	@ use only ttbr0
 		mcrne	p15, 0, r3, c2, c0, 0	@ load page table pointer
+		mcrne	p15, 0, r0, c8, c7, 0	@ flush I,D TLBs
 		mcrne	p15, 0, r1, c3, c0, 0	@ load domain access control
 		mcrne   p15, 0, r6, c2, c0, 2   @ load ttb control
 #endif
